    "features": "<p>The more bureaucracy exists, especially around trade, the more opportunity for someone who skirts shipping regulations. Smugglers are adept at moving contraband from one location to another or helping someone avoid tariffs on goods when the authorities wants their cut. Knowing whose palm to grease and how to talk your way out of a situation are essential, and for smugglers who work alone, knowing who to trust is key. Some smugglers prefer a crew to take on bigger jobs or share the work and risk. What sets a smuggler captain apart from her crew is often the ability to sense an opportunity, weigh the risks, and know when to cut your losses to avoid a ship impound or the kiss of cold vacuum. Too much success can lead to a level of notoriety that makes it difficult to avoid the law—unless a captain can trade via an innocent persona and expert sneakiness.</p><p><strong>Favored Stunts:</strong> Evasive Maneuver, Punch It</p><p><strong>Talents:</strong> Fringer (Novice), Misdirection (Novice)</p><p><strong>Equipment:</strong> hand terminal, padding, pistol, personal ship (with smuggling compartments)</p><p><strong>Armor + Toughness:</strong> 2</p>",
    "statBlockView": true
  },
